TITLE:: PianoRollLoopMarkers
SUMMARY:: Loop start/stop and playback position lines on a piano roll.
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/PianoRollTimeline

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::PianoRollLoopMarkers:: holds three one-pixel-wide LINK::Classes/View:: lines on the roll: loop start and loop end (LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour5::) and a playback head (LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour3::). The playback head defaults to beat zero and is moved with LINK::#-playheadTime_::. LINK::Classes/PianoRoll#-stopRecording:: applies the recorded note range by calling LINK::#-loopStart_::, then LINK::#-playheadTime_:: with the same unsnapped beat argument as LINK::#-loopStart_::, then LINK::#-loopEnd_:: (snapping and ordering rules as for timeline clicks).

Snap resolution for timeline clicks and for LINK::#-playheadTime_:: is stored in the instance variable CODE::prSnapResolutionBeats:: (beats between snap grid points; default one sixteenth note). Clicks are snapped with rounding before the start/end ordering rules are applied.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a TELETYPE::PianoRollLoopMarkers::. The line LINK::Classes/View::s are created on the first successful call to LINK::#-playheadTime_::, LINK::#-loopStart_::, or LINK::#-loopEnd_::.

ARGUMENT:: parent
The roll surface (typically the piano roll LINK::Classes/UserView::) on which the lines are parented.

ARGUMENT:: horizontalScale
Pixels per beat, matching the roll's horizontal scale.

ARGUMENT:: rollHeight
Height of the lines in pixels (typically the full roll height).

ARGUMENT:: palette
A LINK::Classes/GuiPalette::; loop markers use LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour5:: and the playback line uses LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour3::.

ARGUMENT:: defaultStopBeat
Initial loop end beat before any marker is set (for example the roll length in beats). Pass nil to use a built-in default.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: loopEnd
The loop end beat. Reading returns the current end marker. Setting snaps the given beat using CODE::prSnapResolutionBeats::, then sets the end marker if the snapped beat is strictly after the current start marker. Otherwise posts a warning and does nothing. Also used when LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: applies the recorded range after LINK::#-stopRecording::. On success, invokes the function registered with LINK::#-onLoopEndMove_::, if any, passing the snapped beat.

ARGUMENT:: rawBeat
Unsnapped beat position when setting (e.g. from a timeline click or from recorded note timing).

RETURNS::
The current loop end beat.

METHOD:: loopStart
The loop start beat. Reading returns the current start marker. Setting snaps the given beat using CODE::prSnapResolutionBeats::, then sets the start marker if the snapped beat is strictly before the current end marker. Otherwise posts a warning and does nothing. Also used when LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: applies the recorded range after LINK::#-stopRecording::. On success, invokes the function registered with LINK::#-onLoopStartMove_::, if any, passing the snapped beat.

ARGUMENT:: rawBeat
Unsnapped beat position when setting (e.g. from a timeline click or from recorded note timing).

RETURNS::
The current loop start beat.

METHOD:: onLoopEndMove_
Registers a function called when LINK::#-loopEnd_:: successfully moves the end marker. The function receives the snapped end beat in beats. Returns this instance for chaining.

ARGUMENT:: action
A LINK::Classes/Function:: invoked after a successful loop-end move.

METHOD:: onLoopStartMove_
Registers a function called when LINK::#-loopStart_:: successfully moves the start marker. The function receives the snapped start beat in beats. Returns this instance for chaining.

ARGUMENT:: action
A LINK::Classes/Function:: invoked after a successful loop-start move.

METHOD:: playheadTime_
Stores the playback position and refreshes all three marker LINK::Classes/View::s using the same internal update as LINK::#-loopStart_:: and LINK::#-loopEnd_:: (so the playback line is created even when the loop bounds have not been set yet). When CODE::snap:: is true, snaps the given beat the same way as LINK::#-loopStart_:: (using CODE::prSnapResolutionBeats::).

ARGUMENT:: rawBeat
Unsnapped playback position in beats.

ARGUMENT:: snap
When true (default), snap CODE::rawBeat:: to the grid defined by CODE::prSnapResolutionBeats::; when false, store CODE::rawBeat:: verbatim.

PRIVATE:: init, prSnapBeat, prUpdateLineViews
